<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0697">Remark <span data-tag="0697">11.4.0.9</span>.</a> The converse of Lemma <a data-tag="05Z1" href="/tag/05Z1">6.2.4.1</a> is true as well: if $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$ is a reflective subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$, then the collection of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$-local equivalences satisfies conditions $(1)$ through $(4)$. Condition $(3)$ is tautology, condition $(4)$ is a reformulation of the assumption that $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}'$ is reflective, and conditions $(1)$ and $(2)$ follow from Remarks <a data-tag="05YU" href="/tag/05YU">6.2.2.4</a> and <a data-tag="05YV" href="/tag/05YV">6.2.2.5</a>, respectively. </p>
